A||||6||JetroGT||Head liner question||||5||
Z||000000||JetroGT||09-13-2001||11:30 PM||||I just recovered the headliner on my GT, no sunroof.<BR>How long should I wait before reinstalling it?||||reg||5
Z||000001||JayUSA77||09-14-2001||01:10 AM||||i put mine back in in about 10 min and it looks great too <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||09-14-2001||02:17 PM||||I did mine last year in the summer. I put it right back in and it sagged within 6 months.<BR> I piled all of my laundry on top of it over night. That should do it.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Liner.jpg"> <P>I'm using the Fiero store fiberglass back board. I'm leaving out the coat hangers.<p>[This message has been edited by JetroGT (edited 09-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||09-14-2001||08:10 PM||||You might want to reconsider the coat hangers.  They help support the headliner.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||09-15-2001||06:02 PM||||Ill bet you used spray can glue. I only use linoleum contact cement. It will never ever come back down, guarranteed. I tried to get it down to cover it in vinyl after 3 years, but gave up and covered rite over it instead. I put the contact cement in a spray gun unthinned and spray it like thick paint on both surfaces. It comes out all stringy like, not wet enough to soak thru material.||||reg||1
Z||000005||truxpin||09-15-2001||06:38 PM||||getroGT,<P>In a few week I take delivery on my '87 GT, the first thing I'm gonna need to do is fix sagging headliner.(something I've never done is remove one before)<BR>I'm pretty sure I can get it in and out of there , but don't want to screw it up.  Any tricks I should know of before I dig into it? <BR>Thanks for any tips!<BR>truxpin<P>------------------<BR>Hopefully I can put a pic of my '87 GT in here soon!!<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/royalstartourdeluxe/webbike.JPG">   <P>[This message has been edited by truxpin (edited 09-15-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by truxpin (edited 09-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||JetroGT||09-15-2001||09:32 PM||||Heres what I did. I removed the visors dome light, 3rd brake light, passenger side seat, all the door trim on that side. Be careful not to break the roof trim along the head liner. The tabs break off easy. When removing the visors you might damage the board. <BR>I also removed the inner sail panel. Two torx hold the seat belt down. Then I slid the head liner out. <BR>I gotta go back to work. Might be back in 2 hours.||||reg||1
